# study.export
# Example export file. VS Code Aster can help you create an .export:
# https://github.com/simvia-tech/vs-code-aster (open-source, maintained by Simvia - https://simvia.tech)
# Do not set mpi_nbcpu or ncpus here: csauto ignores them and sets them at launch from n and nt.

# Simulation parameters
P time_limit 300
P memory_limit 1024
P mpi_nbnoeud 1

# Input files
F comm study.comm D 1
F mmed ../MESH/{mesh_name} D 20

# Output files
F rmed RESU/myresults.rmed R 80
F mess output.mess R 6
